# 2026-08-30 01:14:43.376357
+Task: Upgrade and configure the codebase to support an interactive, auto-adjusting, real 3D model visualization system with dynamic long arrow callouts and HTML/CSS labels.
+​1. Dependency Management
+​Inspect package.json. If any of the following packages are present, update them to their latest compatible versions. If they are missing, install them:
+​Core 3D Pipeline: three, @react-three/fiber, @react-three/drei
+​Animation & UI: gsap, lucide-react, tailwindcss, clsx, tailwind-merge
+​Developer Types: @types/three, @types/react, @types/react-dom, typescript
+​Run the package manager installation (npm install, pnpm install, or yarn) to apply updates.
+​2. Architectural Requirements
+​No 2D Canvas Fallbacks: Render the object strictly using WebGL/WebGPU in Three.js/R3F.
+​Real 3D Arrows: Use vector lines (@react-three/drei <Line/> or THREE.ArrowHelper) connected directly between origin points on the 3D model mesh and outer targeted coordinate vectors.
+​Auto-Adjusting Labels: Attach screen-space UI overlays using @react-three/drei <Html/> anchored to the 3D tip of each line. Ensure labels auto-project correctly across zoom, pan, and orbital rotation.
+​Smooth Animations: Integrated gsap for camera focus transitions, exploded mesh animations, and arrow pointer scaling upon part selection.
+​3. Output Requirements
+​Execute the terminal commands to install/upgrade the dependencies.
+​Create or update a dedicated component (e.g., AnnotatedModelViewer.tsx) implementing a working prototype containing a sample mesh, dynamic long arrows, and responsive CSS labels. 

